; regression test: a `local`-labelled `def` whose symbol is required by an exported fact is
; rejected with a clear error -- exporting a fact that mentions a symbol without exporting
; what that symbol even *means* would silently smuggle out something the theory author
; explicitly marked private. This fires even when the file is checked directly (not loaded
; by anything else): `load_file`/`merge_and_pop` run uniformly whether this file is the
; top-level file being checked or a dependency of another file, so the file's own internal
; export consistency is checked regardless of how it's invoked. See
; doc/kurt-soundness.md #7.
load prop
bool P
use P  local "p-holds"
def Q iff P  local "hidden"
use Q implies P  "exported-leak"
;;; EvalError: symbol(s) ['Q'] are defined `local` but required by an exported fact -- export their `def` too, or keep them out of exported facts
